# Mirror / archive controls.
#
# Files marked `export-ignore` are excluded from `git archive` output (the
# tarballs/zips produced by GitHub release downloads or `git archive HEAD`).
# This is a defensive line of protection for content that should stay
# internal even when this repo is mirrored or sampled out to a public
# project (e.g. the public github.com/intel/sycl-tla mirror).
#
# `export-ignore` does NOT block `git push` to a remote that has the
# corresponding files — for that, the public mirror's sync configuration
# must filter these paths explicitly. Treat this file as belt-and-suspenders.

# In-repo agent skills. Some skills (e.g. cutlass-jira, cutlass-confluence-wiki)
# describe internal-only infrastructure and are not useful publicly.
.claude/                                   export-ignore
